# Tier B: the preview pane — an image, code with syntax colouring, two megabytes of text, and the
# same two megabytes as hex.
#
# A selection does not load the preview; a debounce does, a little later, off-thread. So each sample
# chains the selection with `settle-preview`, which waits for that load to start and finish, and the
# number is "clicked to shown" rather than "clicked".

preview-fixture
write Preview/Big.txt 2000000
write-binary Preview/Big.bin 2000000
go Preview
preview on
time preview.png select sample.png; settle-preview
assert-preview image
time preview.code select Sample.cs; settle-preview
assert-preview text
time preview.text2mb select Big.txt; settle-preview
assert-preview text
time preview.hex2mb select Big.bin; preview-mode hex; settle-preview
assert-preview hex
preview-mode auto
mem preview
assert-not-launched
